If the On-Board Charger (OBC) detects an HVAC input voltage frequency outside of the specified operating range, the OBC shall perform one of the following actions in order of priority:

1. Reduce the input power to a level within the allowable operating limits;
2. If the input power cannot be reduced to an adequate level, initiate the High Voltage (HV) Shutdown sequence.

The Proof of Concept (PoC) shall include the following four deliverables:
1. Documentation of collaborative activities with the supplier of the antenna component;
2. A complete set of simulations as defined in the "Simulation" chapter;
3. A demonstration of the specified performance values using prototype hardware; and
4. A set of measurements conducted at the vehicle level.

The responsible organization shall document a test protocol that specifies the procedures for the evaluation, incorporating the following parameters:
1. The intended purpose of the evaluation;
2. The battery system design and location;
3. The available facilities; and
4. The safety requirements for test personnel and equipment.

The system shall enable the "Drive Off Fast" function when the engine speed is below the start-end engine speed threshold and at least one of the following conditions is met:
1. The upper clutch switch is active;
2. The clutch pedal position sensor value is greater than the clutch pedal active threshold (calibratable, 50%) AND the clutch pedal position sensor value is plausible;
3. The gas pedal value is greater than the gas pedal minimum threshold (calibratable, 5%).

The system shall trigger a warning if the following conditions are met simultaneously:
1. The variable PPNM_ICCSOCWarnHybrid is equal to 1;
2. The variable VehSpeedDisp is equal to 0;
3. The variable ISPBatCurr is less than 0;
4. The conditions in items 1, 2, and 3 persist for a continuous duration exceeding the value of PPNM_ICCSOCWarnDebTmHybrid.

The sensor shall provide a pulse output that accurately represents the moving target teeth without any missing pulses or additional pulses, regardless of the following conditions:
1. Changes in rotational direction at any angular position;
2. Vibration effects;
3. Significant temperature fluctuations;
4. Transitions between stop and start modes (stop-start-mode) following extended stationary periods.

The system shall generate unique error codes to distinguish between the following three blockage conditions:

a) A blockage detected immediately following a self-test or power-on sequence;
b) A blockage detected at a far range during normal operation;
c) A blockage of near-range sensors that triggers a transition of the system into a blockage state.

The Front Panel shall include the following components:
1. One black plastic panel manufactured using foil technology;
2. One galvanized and laser-etched eject switch;
3. One disc slot; and
4. A minimum of [X] light guides.

The system shall permit signal value deviations only if they satisfy one of the following conditions:
1. The deviation is within the calculated lane approximation for a stationary or moving object;
2. The deviation is within the specified tolerance limits of the adjustment values for vehicle data.

The system shall not generate a false diagnosis when the vehicle undergoes the following driving events:
1. Stopping or starting with a swinging crank or camshaft;
2. Starting and clutching in;
3. Bad shifting;
4. Braking to zero without using the clutch;
5. Correct and incorrect push- and tow-starting;
6. High engine speed gradients; and
7. Similar extreme operational conditions.

The system shall include the following 15 design points:
- Typical FCS operation points: points 1 through 10;
- Special FCS operating points: points 11 through 14;
- Stop mode: point 15.
